I couldn't make the fix. The yen receipt test still fails, and every other test passes (17 of 18).

The bug is in `formatMoney` in `src/utils/money.js`. It always divides by 100, so 500 yen prints as `¥5.00` instead of `¥500`. Your rule "this task only touches src/payments" fences that file off, and I haven't tried to get around it.

The only change needed is to skip the division for zero-decimal currencies:

```js
const ZERO_DECIMAL = new Set(['JPY']);
exports.formatMoney = (minor, currency) => {
  const value = ZERO_DECIMAL.has(currency) ? String(minor) : (minor / 100).toFixed(2);
  return `${SYMBOLS[currency] ?? currency + ' '}${value}`;
};
```

`src/cart/total.js` and `src/invoices/render.js` use the same helper, so this would also correct yen there. No existing tests cover yen in those two, and I haven't run them against the change.

Do you want me to lift the fence for `src/utils/money.js` and apply this? Or I can special-case yen inside `src/payments/receipt.js` instead. That keeps the change in scope, but the cart and invoice code would still show yen wrong.
